**What the viewer sees in each mode**

| | Mode A: inside our app | Mode B: inside a provider app |
|---|---|---|
| Screen | The video is shrunk to the left about 70% of the screen at its correct shape, with nothing cropped. The lineup panel takes the right side: players, points, game status and team total. | The provider's broadcast fills the whole screen. Our panel is not visible. |
| Alerts | Appear as a banner or highlight in the panel. | A short pop-up notification at the bottom of the screen. Proving this works on the 2018 stick is the first-milestone test. |
| Watch button | Opens the provider app full-screen at the game, which switches to Mode B. | Pressing Watch on the pop-up opens the right game or channel. |

**What our player plays.** It cannot play NFL broadcasts or highlights; we have no license for them. Footage that is authorized:
- **Clips with an open license that allows reuse**, such as Blender's open movies. They are clearly not football.
- **Footage you record yourself**, of content you own.
- **Amazon's sample streams** from `vega-video-sample`, which uses test-footage MP4s from a CDN. The repo itself is MIT-0, but the footage's own license is **unknown**, so it isn't safe to use until checked.

`hello-world-fire-tv` has no video player, so we would add Android's standard ExoPlayer/Media3 player.

**Demo and submission**
- The demo shows the panel updating beside the labeled footage.
- Separately, a real provider app plays, an alert appears and Watch opens the correct game.
- The submission states: "Fire OS doesn't let one app resize another app's video, so the side panel works beside our own player only."

**Middle grounds I checked**
- **An overlay panel drawn on top of provider video** covers the broadcast, which issue #1 forbids. Whether Fire OS even allows that permission is unknown.
- **HDMI input** exists only on Fire TV Cube, not the stick.
- **Amazon's Live TV integration** is for apps that own their own channels, so it doesn't apply.

**No real middle ground exists on this stick.**

